@title Take On The New Task Alongside The Helpers Already Working
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-OURJPP turn-utpfU4; first proposed for: Other helpers are already working on one line of work and a second task is ready.
@why [orchestration/recorded-handoff]

! conclusion: Start the new task in its own place (here, a native prototype that runs in seconds), and say what it shares with the helpers' work.

  + IF:
    The operator accepts the agent's plan and asks it to do the new task while the helpers continue.

  + HOWEVER:
    The two lines may touch the same files or compete for the same resources.

  + THEN:
    Start the new task in its own place (here, a native prototype that runs in seconds), and say what it shares with the helpers' work.

  + BECAUSE:
    The operator has said the helpers keep running, so the new task must not stop or disturb them.
